        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9e670bee-fa89-5190-982c-99375de03484",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dallas Frazier\n- Organizations: The Oak Ridge Boys\n- Products: Fancy Free, \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\", \"Voilá, An American Dream\", Ain't Living Long Like This\n- Topics: album releases, singles, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- In 1978, \"Voilá, An American Dream\" was recorded on the album Ain't Living Long Like This and was released as the B-side to the single \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\".\n- On March 26, 1981, The Oak Ridge Boys released Fancy Free as their fifth country studio album.\n- In 1981, Dallas Frazier's song \"Elvira\" became a famous country and pop hit for The Oak Ridge Boys and is considered one of their signature songs.\n- The songs \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles, but none reached the top 40.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
